<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Local XSS Lab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">LOCAL TRAINING ENVIRONMENT</p><h1>XSS Vulnerability Lab</h1>
      <p>Practice finding and explaining reflected, stored, and DOM-based XSS.</p></header>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Safety boundary:</strong> this lab binds to 127.0.0.1. Use harmless proof-of-execution payloads and never test systems without permission.</div>
    <section class="cards">
      <article><span class="tag">Challenge 01</span><h2>Reflected XSS</h2><p>Trace a URL parameter into the HTML response.</p><a href="/reflected?q=hello">Open challenge →</a></article>
      <article><span class="tag">Challenge 02</span><h2>Stored XSS</h2><p>Submit a comment and see how saved content is rendered.</p><a href="/stored">Open challenge →</a></article>
      <article><span class="tag">Challenge 03</span><h2>DOM-based XSS</h2><p>Follow URL fragment data into a browser DOM sink.</p><a href="/dom">Open challenge →</a></article>
    </section>
    <h2>Hunter workflow</h2>
    <ol><li>Identify input sources: query strings, forms, URL fragments.</li><li>Trace where input goes: HTML, attributes, JavaScript, or DOM sinks.</li><li>Test only with harmless proof-of-execution payloads.</li><li>Record impact, reproduction steps, and a remediation.</li></ol>
  </main>
</body></html>